--TEST--
In a `propertyPath<T>`, `@key` or `@value` after something that is not an array, a part after `@key`, and any other word that starts with `@` is the unknown-member error at that part — `rule:types/property-path`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `@key` and `@value` are allowed only after an array.
class Author {
    public string $name = "Ada";
}

class Book {
    public string $title = "Novis";
    public array<Author> $authors = [];
    public ?Author $editor = null;
}

class Shelf {
    public static function sortBy(propertyPath<Book> $path): string {
        return "sorted by " . ($path as string);
    }
}

// `title` is a `string`, not an array.
echo Shelf::sortBy("title.@key"), "\n";
// `editor` is an `Author`, not an array.
echo Shelf::sortBy("editor.@value"), "\n";
// A path starts at the class `Book`, which is not an array.
echo "@key" as propertyPath<Book> as string, "\n";
// `@key` is the last part of a path.
echo Shelf::sortBy("authors.@key.name"), "\n";
// The steps are written in lowercase.
echo Shelf::sortBy("authors.@Key"), "\n";
// `@index` is not a step.
echo Shelf::sortBy("authors.@index"), "\n";
// A lone `@` is not a step.
echo Shelf::sortBy("authors.@"), "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `$title` is not an array, so the path cannot take `@key` after it
   --> %s:20:27
   |
20 | echo Shelf::sortBy("title.@key"), "\n";
   |                           ^^^^ this part of the path is checked here
   = help: `@key` and `@value` follow a property whose type is an array

error[E0405]: `$editor` is not an array, so the path cannot take `@value` after it
   --> %s:22:28
   |
22 | echo Shelf::sortBy("editor.@value"), "\n";
   |                            ^^^^^^ this part of the path is checked here
   = help: `@key` and `@value` follow a property whose type is an array

error[E0405]: `Book` is a class, so the path cannot start with `@key`
   --> %s:24:7
   |
24 | echo "@key" as propertyPath<Book> as string, "\n";
   |       ^^^^ this part of the path is checked here
   = help: `@key` and `@value` follow a property whose type is an array

error[E0405]: `@key` ends a property path, so nothing can follow it
   --> %s:26:29
   |
26 | echo Shelf::sortBy("authors.@key.name"), "\n";
   |                             ^^^^ the path continues after this step
   = help: `@key` is an array element's key, which has no properties

error[E0405]: a property path has no step `@Key`
   --> %s:28:29
   |
28 | echo Shelf::sortBy("authors.@Key"), "\n";
   |                             ^^^^ this part of the path is checked here
   = help: an array's steps are `@key` and `@value`

error[E0405]: a property path has no step `@index`
   --> %s:30:29
   |
30 | echo Shelf::sortBy("authors.@index"), "\n";
   |                             ^^^^^^ this part of the path is checked here
   = help: an array's steps are `@key` and `@value`

error[E0405]: a property path has no step `@`
   --> %s:32:29
   |
32 | echo Shelf::sortBy("authors.@"), "\n";
   |                             ^ this part of the path is checked here
   = help: an array's steps are `@key` and `@value`

